## Source
Path A UX dry-run (0152), severity: **High**

## Context (reimagined)
The tag `2026-05-30` IS a real signed release tag (verified: `git ls-remote
--tags origin`). The URL works and fetches a binary the maintainer attested.
The original concern (404 or stale binary) is unfounded for now.

The real gap: a user reading the README months later doesn't know whether
`2026-05-30` is the latest release. There is no pointer to where newer tags
are announced. The existing prose says "replace 2026-05-30 with the new tag
name" — but doesn't say where to look.

## Fix
Keep the tag-pinned URL (deliberate design, per commit fa16e4b). Add a
one-liner pointing to the releases page or `git tag` so users can discover
the current tag. Clarify that the date IS a release tag, not a writing date.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] curl URL in README install step 2 uses a stable or well-explained ref
- [ ] A developer following the README 3 months from now gets a working binary
